invariant: INV-17
file: tcp_nonblocking_step.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh tcp_nonblocking
reason: step_finished stages the client Finished and switches to the
  application keys without wiping r->hs, so the handshake secrets
  outlive the handshake. The tcp_nonblocking proof asserts that the
  Finished step leaves the handshake state wiped, and fails on this edit.

--- old
    ct_wipe(&r->hs, sizeof r->hs);
    r->hs.t = t;
--- new
    r->hs.t = t;
